  "worked_solution": "We find the total displacement by calculating the definite integral of the velocity.\n\nLet $d$ be the total displacement between $t=1$ and $t=5.$ Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}(\\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt{t-1})\\,\\text{dt} \\\\  & =(t-1)^{3/2}\\,{|}_{1}^{5} \\\\  & =(5-1)^{3/2}-(1-1)^{3/2} \\\\  & =8-0 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
